  "selection_rationale": [
    "Retain the nine previously exercised primary files and add constructs.lua, closure.lua, pm.lua and math.lua, exactly as approved by the maintainer.",
    "Retain bwcoercion.lua as an unchanged required helper, with distinct six-handler/fallback/caller-location witness inside bitwise process evidence rather than another primary-file claim.",
    "Default and upstream-test are separately measured semantic/ABI configurations. Every selected T-only assertion executes in its applicable instrumented contexts; default omission reports remain explicit provenance and cannot discharge those bodies.",
    "The scoped public-header ledger selects actual direct C consumers/drivers and inherited GC/IO obligations. It does not certify the global API ledger or unrelated C ABI paths.",
    "lua_getlocal, lua_setlocal and lua_load remain global pending API obligations: the selected Ada Lua-level inspection and loading paths do not call those public C exports. lua_rotate remains selected because the actual lua_remove macro calls it; LUA_ERRMEM is selected for actual refusal/status checks.",
    "Hash-bound source classification and per-process native profile/condition evidence preserve inactive native alternatives as reviewed references, with no assertion-execution pass for a false guard."
  ],
  "acceptance_limits": [
    "This is an author selection proposal, not independent selection approval or runtime evidence.",
    "The contract index remains pending and diagnostic until independently reviewed real C/Ada observations and coverage adjudication are available.",
    "Complete bounded acceptance requires all 26 contexts, exact executable/runtime/oracle identity, named public C and AUnit witness replay, both constructs templates, balanced physical shutdown and independent final reconciliation.",
    "Full M3, unselected primary files, all.lua, heavy.lua and unrelated ecosystem/native-module acceptance remain open."
  ],
